  "title": "A consolidated presentation of the coprime counting dichotomies",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "A self-contained, corrected presentation (presentation.md) of the counting dichotomy for G = N x| C_r (N of exponent p and class c < p, r | p - 1) on closed 3-manifolds with H1(M; F_p) = 0 and boundedly many sectors: the polynomial side in every class (no grading); hardness for every graded class-at-most-4 algebra whose criterion fails at an occurring sector order with the pair condition holding, for every class-2 algebra, and the cross-layer example; the remaining case (pair failures in classes 3 and 4) stated as open. It incorporates the reversed Artin-product identity, the sector-count assumption, the per-group anchor isolation and the interpretation boundary, and separates uniform proof obligations, classical ingredients, literature and finite validation. Frozen predecessors are unchanged (hashes checked).",
